diff --git a/saas/README.md b/saas/README.md
index 28b0891..aa10a14 100644
--- a/saas/README.md
+++ b/saas/README.md
@@ -24,6 +24,26 @@ After making changes to this gem, you need to update Fizzy to pick up the change
 BUNDLE_GEMFILE=Gemfile.saas bundle update --conservative fizzy-saas
 ```
 
+## Billing
+
+Hosted Fizzy is paid, with three plans:
+
+| Plan       | Price      | Cards     | Storage |
+| ---------- | ---------- | --------- | ------- |
+| Free       | —          | 1,000     | 1 GB    |
+| Unlimited  | $20/month  | Unlimited | 5 GB    |
+| Unlimited+ | $25/month  | Unlimited | 500 GB  |
+
+The plans live in `app/models/plan.rb`. Stripe hosts checkout and the customer
+portal, and posts subscription changes to `/stripe/webhooks`, which is the only
+thing that writes `account_subscriptions`. Four environment variables configure
+the integration: `STRIPE_SECRET_KEY`, `STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET`,
+`STRIPE_MONTHLY_V1_PRICE_ID`, and `STRIPE_MONTHLY_EXTRA_STORAGE_V1_PRICE_ID`.
+
+An account that runs out of cards can still draft, but publishing and creating
+through the API are refused until it upgrades. Support can comp an account or
+override its usage numbers from `/admin/accounts`.
+
 ## Working with Stripe
 
